ilestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pyca/cryptography/milestones/17","html_url":"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/milestone/17","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pyca/cryptography/milestones/17/labels","id":1807924,"node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lMTgwNzkyNA==","number":17,"title":"Fifteenth release","description":"","creator":{"login":"alex","id":772,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/772?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alex","html_url":"https://github.com/alex","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alex/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alex/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alex/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alex/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alex/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alex/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alex/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alex/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alex/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":45,"state":"closed","created_at":"2016-06-03T20:34:45Z","updated_at":"2016-08-26T15:00:01Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2016-08-26T15:00:01Z"},"comments":4,"created_at":"2016-07-28T06:38:53Z","updated_at":"2020-08-15T00:02:19Z","closed_at":"2016-08-02T01:08:21Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":"resolved","sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5280  4.1.2.2.  Serial Numbers\n\n`Conforming CAs MUST NOT  use serialNumber values longer than 20 octets.`\n\nWell, let's look to source code:\n\ncryptography/hazmat/backends/openssl/backend.py :\n\n``` python\ndef _int_to_bn(self, num, bn=None):\n    ...\n    binary = num.to_bytes(int(num.bit_length() / 8.0 + 1), \"big\")\n    ...\n```\n\ncryptography/x509/base.py:\n\n``` python\nclass CertificateBuilder:\n    def serial_number(self, number):\n        if utils.bit_length(number) > 160\n```\n\nSince serial number should be positive, for my example below it should add additional zero.\n\nSample program:\n\n``` python\nimport datetime\nfrom cryptography import x509\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.backends import default_backend\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives import serialization\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.asymmetric import rsa\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.hashes import SHA256\nfrom cryptography.x509 import NameOID\nkey = rsa.generate_private_key(public_exponent=65537, key_size=512, backend=default_backend())\nserial = int.from_bytes(b'\\xff' * 20, 'big')\nsubj = x509.Name([x509.NameAttribute(NameOID.COMMON_NAME, 'qwe')])\nbuilder = x509.CertificateBuilder()\nbuilder = builder.subject_name(subj)\nbuilder = builder.issuer_name(subj)\nbuilder = builder.not_valid_before(datetime.datetime.today())\nbuilder = builder.not_valid_after(datetime.datetime.today())\nbuilder = builder.serial_number(serial)\nbuilder = builder.public_key(key.public_key())\ncert = builder.sign(private_key=key, algorithm=SHA256(), backend=default_backend())\nprint(cert.public_bytes(encoding=serialization.Encoding.PEM).decode('ascii'))\n```\n\n`./qwe.py | openssl asn1parse -inform pem  -i` gives:\n\n```\n...\n13:d=2  hl=2 l=  21 prim:   INTEGER           :FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF\n...\n```\n\nNote 21 byte (!)\n","closed_by":{"login":"reaperhulk","id":161495,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161495?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/reaperhulk","html_url":"https://github.com/reaperhulk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reaperhulk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.co